<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Privacy Policy</title>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f7f5f2 0%, #eef7f5 100%);
      color: #1f2937;
    }
    .privacy-shell {
      max-width: 980px;
      margin: 3rem auto;
      padding: 2rem 1.35rem 3rem;
    }
    .privacy-card {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);
      border: 1px solid rgba(148,163,184,0.2);
      border-radius: 24px;
      box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(15,23,42,0.07);
      padding: 2rem 2.2rem;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    }
    .meta {
      color: #475569;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    h2 {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: #111827;
    }
    p, li {
      color: #334155;
      line-height: 1.75;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    ul {
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0 1.2rem;
    }
    .back-link {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 2rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #0f766e;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="privacy-shell">
    <div class="privacy-card">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="meta">Effective date: September 2, 2026</div>

      <p>This application is designed to support academic hiring and faculty recruitment workflows. We collect and process information only as needed to provide job discovery, resume review, shortlist handling, interviews, and user account access.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account information such as name, email, password hash, and role.</li>
        <li>Profile and resume information, including skills, experience, qualifications, and uploaded CV/resume files.</li>
        <li>Job application data, hiring status, interview history, and meeting records.</li>
        <li>System activity such as login timestamps, device/browser metadata, and form submissions used for operational logging.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use the information</h2>
      <p>We use personal data to authenticate users, manage job applications, evaluate candidate fit, generate shortlist and interview workflows, support HR/admin review, and improve the quality of job matching and hiring insights.</p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>We retain data only as long as needed for account management, recruitment operations, record keeping, and legal or compliance requirements. Resume backups and hiring records may be kept for operational continuity.</p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>We use standard web security practices to protect stored user data and authentication, including password hashing and secure session handling. However, no internet-connected system is completely immune to risk, and users should avoid submitting unnecessary sensitive information.</p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell personal data. Information may be shared only with authorized recruiters, admins, or internal personnel involved in the hiring workflow.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information associated with your account, subject to operational and legal requirements. Contact the administrator or platform owner for those requests.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>We may use cookies or session storage for authentication, user session continuity, and app functionality. You can disable or manage cookies in your browser settings, but some features may not work properly without them.</p>

      <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to home</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
